Q3. Would you use LinkedList for 5 million books?

It depends on the application's access pattern.
If I frequently access books by index or search through them,
I would still prefer ArrayList.
If I already have references to nodes and perform many insertions and deletions in the middle,
LinkedList could be beneficial. However, for most real-world Java applications,
ArrayList is usually the preferred choice because of better cache locality and faster iteration.